WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.663
Why start with an inventory?

2
00:00:01.663 --> 00:00:03.875
Because you can't fix what you can't list.

3
00:00:03.875 --> 00:00:08.690
A role reaches a person in four ways
that look the same on an admin's screen

4
00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:13.825
and very different to an attacker:
permanent or time-bound, eligible or active.

5
00:00:13.825 --> 00:00:16.525
An activated role looks
active for a while,

6
00:00:16.525 --> 00:00:19.225
and a role on a group
reaches everyone in it.

7
00:00:19.225 --> 00:00:24.318
Microsoft's own target is zero permanently
active assignments outside the emergency

8
00:00:24.318 --> 00:00:28.987
accounts, and the program wants roles to
reach people only through named groups.

9
00:00:28.987 --> 00:00:31.093
So the first gate is simply this:

10
00:00:31.093 --> 00:00:34.460
know what's standing today,
and classify it by tier.
